# MTK ACCDET (accessory detect) on the PMIC.
#
# This chassis has no 3.5 mm jack -- audio out is the bottom speaker, the
# earpiece and USB-C -- and there is no /sys/class/switch/h2w, so
# WiredAccessoryManager never sees a headset. The driver is nevertheless
# instantiated by the MT6755 PMIC and advertises the full inline-remote key set
# (KEY_VOLUMEUP, KEY_VOLUMEDOWN, KEY_PLAYPAUSE, KEY_VOICECOMMAND) plus the
# SW_*_INSERT switches, all driven by an ADC on jack pins that do not exist.
#
# Under Generic.kl a floating-ADC glitch on that comparator becomes a real
# VOLUME_UP down event. That matters here: a VOLUME_UP down with no matching up
# latches PhoneWindowManager's mA11yShortcutChordVolumeUpKeyTriggered, which
# makes interceptPowerKeyDown() set mPowerKeyHandled and never call
# wakeUpFromPowerKey() -- the "power button does not light the screen" fault.
# ACCDET is one of the two devices that can produce that event, so it is
# neutralised: no scan code is declared, InputReader resolves every one of them
# to AKEYCODE_UNKNOWN and drops it. Raw events stay visible to getevent.
#
# Restore the inline-remote mapping here if a jack is ever confirmed.
